 "task": "Everything for the phone on 1/1/6 looks right: a multi-domain port, an LLDP group for LLDP-MED endpoints, a VOICE role and a device profile. The PC works, the phone never gets VOICE. Turn on debugging for LLDP and port-access, unplug and replug the phone, read the buffer, and fix what it tells you.",
 "hints": [
  "`debug lldp event` and `debug portaccess all`. The buffer is the default destination; `show debug` lists what is on.",
  "Unplug and plug the phone from the Devices panel (or `sim disconnect phone`, `sim connect phone`), then `show debug buffer module lldp`.",
  "`lldp_receive_neighbor_clear: intf 1/1/6` is the switch throwing the phone's LLDP away. The lab switch did exactly this on 2026-09-28.",
  "`aaa authentication port-access allow-lldp-bpdu` on 1/1/6. Then `show debug buffer module portaccess | include DEVICEPROFILE`."
 ],
